    "doc": "ufc_c5isr_facilities",
    "query": "What are the power and grounding requirements for C5ISR systems?",
    "answer": "For C5ISR systems, power and grounding requirements are as follows:\n\n- The power distribution architecture must be implemented to meet the facility Grade requirement. For Army projects, refer to TM 5-691 Utility Systems Design.\n- Systems Manual (SM) requirements must be incorporated by the Designer of Record (DOR) into the design.\n- C5ISR spaces with data equipment must comply with ASHRAE Thermal requirements for air temperature and humidity. Liquid cooling temperature must also comply with these requirements.\n- Controls must account for temperature rise during primary power loss.\n- The design must comply with user criteria and MESEP requirements where more stringent.\n- The building must be able to be disconnected from its main utility power supply and provide independent power to emergency power system controls, mechanical system controls, and other Grade required systems.\n- Grounding and bonding must be provided in accordance with NFPA 70, TIA-607-D, and MIL-STD-188-124B. Grounding is not required in spaces where MIL-STD-188-124B apply.\n- Concrete floors/slab which will increase the design thickness must provide grounding in accordance with Motorola R56, ensuring the subsystem does not exceed 5 ohms.",
